This is the standard source-available software licence for SANSEVIERIA OÜ projects. The same terms may be applied unchanged to multiple projects and releases. It is a standalone licence, not an OSI-approved open-source licence, and does not itself offer an alternative grant under the GNU GPL or AGPL. Separately licensed material and permissions remain subject to their own terms.

1 Definitions and application

Project means a software project or identifiable software component released under this License. This License is not limited to one named application, repository, programming language or type of software. Each Project and release uses the same licence text; its release notice identifies the applicable software, rights holders and separately licensed components without changing these terms.

Application of this License requires a grant by a person entitled to make it. A company-wide licensing policy does not by itself relicense third-party material or withdraw rights previously granted under other terms. The mere presence of a file in a SANSEVIERIA repository does not override an applicable separate licence.

Steward means SANSEVIERIA OÜ, identified in the release notice. The Steward maintains the official project and administers the limited Commercial Authorization mechanism in section 7. Its position does not make it the owner of every Contribution.

Original Software means software that a person entitled to license it expressly makes available under this License and identifies in the applicable release. Modified Version means a work that modifies Original Software or incorporates it into a derivative work, to the extent those modifications or incorporations fall within the rights protected by applicable copyright law. It does not include an independent work merely aggregated with or interoperating with Original Software as described in section 3.

Covered Software means Original Software and the covered portions of Modified Versions, including additions that form part of the derivative work within the preceding definition. Changing a label or omitting a licence notice does not remove a modification from that scope. Separately licensed third-party material retains its own terms; section 5 governs whether a proposed combination can lawfully be distributed. The applicable release must identify the covered files or components and separately licensed material.

Contribution means an original addition or modification to Covered Software that its rights holder intentionally releases under this License. Contributor means that rights holder, or a person authorized to grant the relevant rights on its behalf. A Licensor is a Contributor or other rights holder making a grant under this License. These definitions do not treat unsolicited communications, downloads or mere repository access as contributions or grants.

You means the person exercising rights under this License. A person acting for an organization must have authority to do so. Each separate organization receives its own rights directly under this License; it does not acquire them solely by sharing ownership with another organization.

Corresponding Source means the preferred form for modifying the Covered Software version concerned, together with the source of its covered modifications and the build, installation and execution instructions, interface definitions and scripts reasonably necessary to reproduce and operate that version. It excludes users' data, passwords, private keys and production credentials. Use templates and instructions in place of secrets. Separately licensed general-purpose tools and independent components need not be relicensed under this License, but their identities, versions, required notices and lawful means of obtaining them must be documented where necessary to build or operate the Covered Software.

External Network Use means enabling people outside Your organization to interact with the Covered Software or a material part of its functionality over a network. Your personnel and contractors acting solely for Your internal operations are not external users for that activity. Independent customers and users of a service are external users.

Commercial Offering means an activity described in section 4. Commercial Authorization means a written authorization satisfying section 7. Permission under that section concerns the restrictions in section 4 only.

2 Copyright permission

Subject to this License, each Licensor grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free permission, for the duration of the relevant rights and subject only to the termination provisions below, to run, study, reproduce, modify, display, make available and distribute its Covered Software, in source or executable form, and to make compliant forks.

This permission includes personal use, research and internal business use. It permits private modifications without a duty to publish them merely because they were made. The source obligations in section 5 apply when You distribute Covered Software or enable External Network Use. Commercial Offerings require section 7 authorization unless section 4 expressly permits the activity.

No Licensor grants rights it does not own or control. This License does not require surrender of copyright or moral rights. Except where expressly granted, rights are reserved, without limiting statutory exceptions or other permissions You already hold.

3 Independent works and protected rights

This License does not apply to an independently created program merely because that program communicates with, calls or implements a compatible interface. It does not license or restrict independently created outputs merely because Covered Software was used to produce them. An output or purported independent component containing Covered Software or other protected material remains subject to the applicable rights in that material.

These exclusions do not exempt Your own operation, copying or distribution of Covered Software from this License. For example, a separately developed user interface does not exempt a paid service that You operate using Covered Software from section 4.

The same distinction applies to an independent extension: operating or distributing Covered Software as part of a paid offering can require authorization even where the paid features are implemented by that extension. Selling only an independent extension, without supplying or operating Covered Software, does not by itself make the extension's author subject to this License. A separately licensed component's commercial permissions are not amended by this License; Your own activities involving Covered Software must independently satisfy its conditions.

Nothing restricts observation, study, testing, interoperability, reverse engineering or other acts to the extent applicable law permits them notwithstanding contractual terms. No provision asserts an exclusive right in ideas, functionality or interfaces as such.

4 Commercial scope

Without a Commercial Authorization, You must not:

1. require consideration for a copy, download, licence, distribution or fork of Covered Software;
2. provide Covered Software as a hosted, managed, white-label or other service in return for consideration for access to the software or a material part of its functionality;
3. operate or distribute Covered Software as part of an offering in which payment is required to unlock functionality delivered through that software, including paid integrated extensions or tiers; or
4. condition access to a copy, update or covered functionality on purchasing another product or service, paying a related party, accepting a nominal donation requirement or making a functionally equivalent payment.

Consideration includes fees, royalties, subscriptions and other agreed value provided in exchange for the relevant copy, access or functionality. The payment's label, invoice allocation or recipient does not avoid these restrictions. Ordinary revenue from an independent business that uses Covered Software internally is not, by itself, consideration for Covered Software. Merely using Covered Software to create independent goods, documents, analyses or other outputs does not make their sale a Commercial Offering.

You may charge for separately supplied consulting, training, installation, support or commissioned development if the charge purchases the professional work rather than a right to obtain or use Covered Software, and is not a required purchase for copies or covered functionality that You otherwise offer. Delivering covered modifications to a customer triggers section 5; the customer must receive them under this License without additional licence restrictions. Development work may be paid for even though the resulting covered code is licensed without a licence fee.

A professional-service charge is not separate if You require it, directly or through another person, as a condition of obtaining, activating, updating or ordinarily using a copy or covered functionality that You supply, regardless of the amount or invoice description. This rule does not prevent payment for genuinely commissioned work whose resulting code is delivered under the preceding paragraph.

The professional-services exception does not authorize You to sell access to a hosted instance that You provide or control as a service, even if an equivalent copy can be self-hosted for free. Installation and administration work performed on the customer's infrastructure or cloud account may qualify as professional services when the customer separately obtains the infrastructure and the work does not supply an access subscription. No exception for hosting merely described as dedicated or at cost is implied.

This permitted work may include recurring configuration, monitoring, maintenance and administration performed on the customer's instructions, provided the customer independently contracts and pays for the infrastructure, controls the instance and can replace the contractor without losing the right or practical means to access the Covered Software. Merely placing an account in the customer's name does not turn a subscription controlled and supplied by the provider into professional work.

You may accept genuinely voluntary donations or sponsorship that do not purchase copies, updates, access, features or preferential use of Covered Software. This paragraph does not authorize a paid access tier presented as a donation.

Ordinary advertising displayed alongside genuinely free software access is not, by itself, consideration for that access. This does not exempt a payment that in substance buys access or paid functionality, and it grants no permission to collect, disclose or monetize personal data. This License therefore does not prohibit all revenue-generating activity associated with a free offering.

5 Distribution and source availability

When You distribute Covered Software, You must:

1. supply this License, preserve applicable copyright, licence and attribution notices, identify material modifications and provide a reasonable way to identify the version distributed;
2. license Your covered modifications under this same version of this License and make the grants required by sections 6 and 7 for those modifications;
3. provide the Corresponding Source with the copy or offer it to each recipient through an accessible electronic means without an additional source-access fee; and
4. refrain from imposing additional terms or technical restrictions that prevent recipients from exercising the rights this License grants in Covered Software. This does not prohibit legitimate security controls that leave a practical means to obtain and use the source and exercise those rights.

During External Network Use, give every interacting user a reasonably prominent way to obtain the Corresponding Source of the version actually used, at no additional charge and without requiring purchase of a separate service. Access may require the same account used for the service, but must not require surrender of the rights granted by this License or disclosure of unnecessary personal information.

Keep the source offer available for at least three years after the last distribution of that version by You or the end of its External Network Use by You, whichever is later. Maintain a reliable delivery method during that period. This obligation does not require continued operation of the application service itself.

The source may be supplied to the entitled recipients or users; publication on a public repository is permitted but is not mandatory. Those recipients receive the same rights and may redistribute the source, including to the Steward. You must not prohibit that redistribution. No obligation to submit a pull request or secure a merge decision is created.

These requirements cover only the scope licensed under this License. They do not authorize violation of third-party licence terms. If You cannot satisfy both this License and applicable third-party terms for a proposed combination or distribution, this License does not permit that combination or distribution.

