Each Contributor retains ownership of its Contribution. By intentionally releasing covered modifications under this License, a Contributor grants recipients the copyright permission in section 2, subject to all conditions of this License. Submission to the official repository must include an express, recorded assent to these terms and the limited authority in section 7, made by a person with the necessary authority. Mere publication of a pull request without that assent is not treated by the Steward as permission to merge or authorize commercial use.

For downstream releases, each distributor must be entitled to make the same grants for its covered modifications and include a notice expressly identifying this License as applying to them and affirming the grants in sections 2, 6 and 7. The notice must identify the releasing person or organization and the relevant version; it need not disclose unnecessary personal information or be sent to the Steward. Redistributing another person's work does not create rights that person has not granted. Preserve evidence of the applicable terms and provenance; no general transfer of authorship or ownership is required.

Each Licensor grants, for activities permitted by this License, a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free patent licence under claims it owns or controls that would necessarily be infringed by the Covered Software it makes available, alone or combined with the Covered Software version identified in its applicable release. This includes the Licensor's Original Software as well as its Contributions. It covers making, using, offering, selling and importing to the extent the activity is otherwise permitted here. It does not cover claims infringed only by additional modifications or other combinations, and is not a warranty about third-party patents.

If You initiate, or direct another person to initiate, a claim seeking relief for alleged direct or indirect infringement of patent claims You own or control by Covered Software as provided by a Licensor, that Licensor may terminate its patent permission to You upon written notice, to the extent permitted by applicable law. This includes an affirmative patent counterclaim seeking such relief, but does not include a defence that seeks no relief for infringement by that Covered Software. Copyright permissions and claims against unrelated products are not terminated by this paragraph alone.

7 Limited commercial authorization

Each Licensor that intentionally makes Original Software or Contributions available under this License expressly authorizes the Steward to approve specified activities otherwise restricted by section 4 for that Licensor's covered material. This is a limited authority, not a transfer of copyright or an unrestricted right to relicense. For an offering involving material from multiple Licensors, the authorization is effective only where the Steward has the necessary rights or authority from every relevant rights holder for each covered part; it must not represent that one Contributor's assent covers another's rights.

A Commercial Authorization must be in writing, issued by an authorized representative of the Steward, and identify the authorized person, the covered Project or Projects and releases or another objectively determinable software scope, the permitted commercial activity, duration and any agreed commercial conditions. The Steward may charge for that authorization. Neither negotiations, repository access, silence nor a partner badge constitutes authorization.

Before issuing it, the Steward must keep records supporting its authority for the covered parts concerned and identify to the customer any excluded components or permissions that must be obtained separately. The authorization must state the scope for which the Steward confirms it holds the required rights or authority. This does not require public disclosure of confidential contributor records or personal information.

This authority permits exceptions only to section 4. It does not permit the Steward to waive source availability, reciprocity, notices, recipients' rights, the scope of patent grants or third-party terms, or to issue proprietary sublicences for Contributions. A customer receiving an authorized Commercial Offering retains the source and reuse rights provided by this License; the provider must not charge separately for the source required by section 5.

A Commercial Authorization does not automatically authorize a customer or other recipient to make a further Commercial Offering. That recipient may make free distributions and exercise all other permissions of this License, and may seek its own authorization when needed. This limitation does not restrict any non-waivable statutory right.

An authorization is effective only to the extent the Steward holds the relevant rights or limited authority from the relevant rights holders. It does not cure missing rights in third-party code or Contributions released under other terms. For its own Contributions, the Steward remains the rights holder; this License does not represent that it has transferred its underlying rights to users or contributors.

