This License grants no general permission to use a Licensor's trademarks or imply affiliation, endorsement or certification. Truthful attribution and referential uses permitted by applicable law remain available. Preserve required attribution without presenting a modified version or independent service as an official SANSEVIERIA release or service.

9 Acceptance and reserved statutory rights

This License must be provided or clearly made accessible before You are asked to accept it. You may accept it by express agreement or by performing an act requiring its permissions after notice identifying the licence version and the particular act that constitutes acceptance. A person relying on acceptance by conduct must provide that notice and a practical opportunity to examine and retain the full text before the identified act. Mere viewing of a website or code, receiving a copy without that notice, or silence is not contractual acceptance.

This provision does not require registration with the Steward or collection of identifying information from every recipient. The express assents for Contributions submitted to the official repository and the written Commercial Authorizations must be recorded as described in sections 6 and 7. Other questions of assent and proof are governed by applicable law.

If You do not accept, this document grants no permission for acts requiring the Licensors' authorization. This does not remove statutory rights, rights under another applicable licence or rights that do not require acceptance. Nothing in this License requires payment or individual permission merely to make a compliant free fork or free distribution.

10 Compliance, termination and reinstatement

This License does not authorize activities that fail its applicable conditions. A cure period is not a permission to carry out a prohibited Commercial Offering and does not erase liability for past acts.

No cure period suspends a condition of permission. During cure, You must stop the non-compliant act and take reasonable steps to remedy its consequences; cure does not waive claims for past conduct.

A Licensor may terminate its grants for Your material breach by written notice identifying the breach if You do not cure it within 30 days after receipt. If completion is reasonably impossible within 30 days, You must cease the prohibited activity, begin cure within that period and complete it diligently within a further 30 days, unless a longer period is agreed in writing. This extension does not permit continued unauthorized commercial activity.

Termination for a repeat material breach after a previously cured breach, or for a breach incapable of cure, may take effect on written notice to the extent permitted by applicable law. Lawful interim or urgent relief is not excluded by these procedures.

A Licensor may reinstate its grants in writing after cure. Termination affects only grants made by the Licensor entitled to terminate them; the Steward cannot terminate other Licensors' grants without their authority. Licences already granted to compliant downstream recipients remain unaffected solely by Your breach. Source offers and delivery obligations already triggered by distribution or External Network Use, required notices and accrued claims survive termination to the extent applicable law permits.

No Licensor may revoke a compliant grant under this version merely for convenience or because a later licence version is published. Rights and remedies that applicable law makes non-waivable are preserved.

