To the extent this License forms a contract, its contractual obligations are governed by Estonian law, subject to mandatory rules that apply notwithstanding that choice. This clause does not determine the law governing non-contractual intellectual-property infringement claims; the applicable conflict-of-laws rules remain effective.

For contractual disputes between You acting in a business capacity and the Steward, the competent courts of Estonia have non-exclusive jurisdiction to the extent a valid jurisdiction agreement may be made. This does not exclude another court with jurisdiction under applicable law or determine jurisdiction for claims between other parties.

Consumers retain all non-waivable protections and jurisdiction rights. Where the applicable conflict-of-laws rules protect a consumer under the law that would apply without this choice, choosing Estonian law does not deprive that consumer of those mandatory protections. In particular, this License does not require a consumer to bring proceedings only in Estonia or allow proceedings against a consumer in a forum that mandatory law excludes.

